# The artwork is DERIVED, and deliberately not committed.
#
# `tools_icon_export.py` builds it from Icons/Master icon Default.png,
# flattening the alpha and cropping the master's bevel — see that file,
# which explains why an exported copy in git is a copy that stops matching
# its source. The Contents.json beside this is hand-written and IS
# committed; only the PNG it names is generated.
#
# Put it here before an Xcode build:
#   cd DiceGameCurrent/DiceGameCurrent && python3 tools_icon_export.py
#   cp Icons/export/AppIcon-1024.png \
#      ../../XcodeOnly/Assets.xcassets/AppIcon.appiconset/
#
# Exported to Icons/export and copied, NOT exported straight in here: the
# same run also writes the eleven Messages slots, and an .appiconset with
# PNGs no Contents.json mentions is a pile of "unassigned children"
# warnings on every build.
AppIcon-1024.png
